# (category entity) An armor stand is two cells tall, so a piston head entering the cell above a
# pressure plate shoves it off the plate and another shoves it back, and the plate is never
# touched (a block entering the plate's own cell would break it, and a minecart cannot be pushed off
# a rail without moving the rail). Back on the plate: on in the block-entity phase of the push tick
# (entityInside -> checkPressed), the piston next to it extends the next tick. Off it: the plate
# lets go only at its re-check, 20 gt after it was pressed (BasePressurePlateBlock.tick), however
# soon the stand left.
design designs/gadgets/entity-plate-stand.txt
probe plate 4 1 0
probe q 4 1 1
settle
expect q E
expect plate #
setblock 2 2 0 minecraft:redstone_block
etrace 24
clear 2 2 0
settle
expect q r
expect_entity armor_stand 5.26 1 0.5
setblock 7 2 0 minecraft:redstone_block
etrace 4
expect q E
clear 7 2 0
settle
expect_entity armor_stand 4.74 1 0.5
